    "guidance": "Validated 3/12 (25%); no reliable state-conditioned slice was demonstrated, so keep non-default despite its intended object-selective translation prior. Consider it only when the lid-handle-versus-peg reference is unambiguous and the translated path is reachable, with reference geometry checked at each 8-action chunk. Avoid ambiguous/unusual intermediate states, arbitrary peg-rotation changes, and recovery from miss, drop, or cover closure. Of the 9 failures, 5 retained an open cover but had retrieve_peg_from_box=false with only 0-0.0124 m reported peg movement; the other 4 ended with the cover effectively closed after 0.730-0.773 m reported peg movement. IK-unconverged steps occurred in 6/12 runs, including all four of those cover-closed/high-movement failures. Recognize failure from a reference-induced target jump, continued lid attachment, offset descent, peg staying low or separating from the TCP, cover angle <=0.9 rad, or persistent IK/limit issues. Handoff to reorient_and_stage_peg only on closed fingers, peg above the wall with margin, and stable two-frame co-motion; validated completion additionally requires peg center >=0.15 m (or insertion) and cover >0.9 rad."
